19:["$","$L1c",null,{"mb":4,"children":[["$","$L1d",null,{"variant":"h2","component":"h1","color":"primary","gutterBottom":true,"children":"Automation glossary"}],["$","$L1d",null,{"textAlign":"justify","color":"text.secondary","children":"The words of industrial automation explained simply: GRAFCET, Ladder, variables, timers, counters. Each term is defined in a few sentences, with a diagram when it helps."}]]}]
1a:["$","$L1e",null,{"sections":[{"id":"general","title":"General concepts"},{"id":"grafcet","title":"GRAFCET"},{"id":"ladder","title":"Ladder"},{"id":"ladder-advanced","title":"Ladder: time, counting and calculation"}],"entries":[{"id":"action","section":"grafcet","term":"Action","aliases":[],"definition":"A rectangle attached to a step: what the system does while the step is active, such as turning an output on.","definitionHtml":"<p>A rectangle attached to a step: what the system does while the step is active, such as turning an output on.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>An action can be continuous, stored (Set / Reset), conditional, delayed or time-limited.</p>\n","searchText":"action","figure":{"src":"/glossary/grafcet/action-en.svg","alt":"A step numbered 1 linked to an action rectangle `pump` on its right.","width":300},"related":[{"id":"step","term":"Step"},{"id":"set-action","term":"Stored action"},{"id":"output","term":"Output"}]},{"id":"and","section":"general","term":"AND","aliases":["in series"],"definition":"An operator that is true only if all its conditions are true.","definitionHtml":"<p>An operator that is true only if all its conditions are true.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>In Ladder, AND corresponds to contacts in series.</p>\n","searchText":"and","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"or","term":"OR"},{"id":"not","term":"NOT"},{"id":"series-parallel","term":"Contacts in series and in parallel"}]},{"id":"and-divergence","section":"grafcet","term":"AND divergence","aliases":["simultaneous sequences","parallelism"],"definition":"A point where the sequence splits into several branches that all start at the same time and then evolve independently.","definitionHtml":"<p>A point where the sequence splits into several branches that all start at the same time and then evolve independently.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>A single transition above the double bar crosses it.</p>\n","searchText":"and divergence","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"or-divergence","term":"OR divergence"},{"id":"convergence","term":"Convergence"}]},{"id":"branch","section":"grafcet","term":"Branch","aliases":[],"definition":"One of the sequences starting from a divergence.","definitionHtml":"<p>One of the sequences starting from a divergence.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"branch","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"divergences","term":"Divergence and convergence"}]},{"id":"coil","section":"ladder","term":"Coil","aliases":["output coil"],"definition":"A symbol at the end of a network that writes a variable: it takes the value of the contact path before it.","definitionHtml":"<p>A symbol at the end of a network that writes a variable: it takes the value of the contact path before it.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>It is used to drive an output or an internal memory.</p>\n","searchText":"coil","figure":{"src":"/glossary/ladder/coil-en.svg","alt":"A minimal network: a `start` contact followed by a `pump` coil, between the two rails.","width":300},"related":[{"id":"contact","term":"Contact"},{"id":"network","term":"Network"},{"id":"output","term":"Output"}]},{"id":"contact","section":"ladder","term":"Contact","aliases":["NO contact","NC contact"],"definition":"A symbol that reads a variable. An NO contact (normally open) conducts when its variable is true; an NC contact (normally closed) conducts when it is false.","definitionHtml":"<p>A symbol that reads a variable. An NO contact (normally open) conducts when its variable is true; an NC contact (normally closed) conducts when it is false.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>The contact reflects the behaviour wanted in the program, not the physical wiring of the button.</p>\n","searchText":"contact","figure":{"src":"/glossary/ladder/contacts-en.svg","alt":"Two contacts: an NO contact, two vertical bars, and an NC contact, two bars with a diagonal.","width":380},"related":[{"id":"coil","term":"Coil"},{"id":"wiring","term":"Wiring: normally open (NO) and normally closed (NC)"},{"id":"series-parallel","term":"Contacts in series and in parallel"}]},{"id":"contactor","section":"general","term":"Contactor","aliases":[],"definition":"A power switch driven by a coil: it lets a low-power output control a motor or a large load.","definitionHtml":"<p>A power switch driven by a coil: it lets a low-power output control a motor or a large load.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"contactor","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"output","term":"Output"}]},{"id":"series-parallel","section":"ladder","term":"Contacts in series and in parallel","aliases":["in series","in parallel"],"definition":"Contacts in series (one after the other) form an AND; contacts in parallel (on two paths) form an OR.","definitionHtml":"<p>Contacts in series (one after the other) form an AND; contacts in parallel (on two paths) form an OR.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"contacts in series and in parallel","figure":{"src":"/glossary/ladder/series-parallel-en.svg","alt":"Two networks: contacts a and b in series equal a AND b, the same contacts in parallel equal a OR b.","width":420},"related":[{"id":"and","term":"AND"},{"id":"or","term":"OR"}]},{"id":"convergence","section":"grafcet","term":"Convergence","aliases":[],"definition":"A point where branches join back. In AND, the sequence continues only once all branches have arrived; in OR, as soon as one branch arrives.","definitionHtml":"<p>A point where branches join back. In AND, the sequence continues only once all branches have arrived; in OR, as soon as one branch arrives.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"convergence","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"divergences","term":"Divergence and convergence"},{"id":"branch","term":"Branch"}]},{"id":"conversion","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Conversion","aliases":["widening","narrowing","*_TO_*"],"definition":"Changing the type of a value. A widening (INT to DINT) is safe; a narrowing (REAL to INT) can lose information and must be requested explicitly.","definitionHtml":"<p>Changing the type of a value. A widening (INT to DINT) is safe; a narrowing (REAL to INT) can lose information and must be requested explicitly.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"conversion","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"data-type","term":"Type"}]},{"id":"counter","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Counter","aliases":["CTU","CTD","CTUD","counting up","counting down"],"definition":"A block that counts rising edges. CTU increments on CU, CTD decrements on CD (with LD to load the PV value), CTUD does both. The current value is on the CV pin.","definitionHtml":"<p>A block that counts rising edges. CTU increments on CU, CTD decrements on CD (with LD to load the PV value), CTUD does both. The current value is on the CV pin.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"counter","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"preset-value","term":"Preset value"},{"id":"function-block","term":"Function block"},{"id":"rising-edge","term":"Rising edge"}]},{"id":"directed-link","section":"grafcet","term":"Directed link","aliases":[],"definition":"A line joining steps and transitions, read from top to bottom. An arrow is drawn only when it goes back up.","definitionHtml":"<p>A line joining steps and transitions, read from top to bottom. An arrow is drawn only when it goes back up.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"directed link","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"step","term":"Step"},{"id":"transition","term":"Transition"}]},{"id":"divergences","section":"grafcet","term":"Divergence and convergence","aliases":["junction","bar"],"definition":"A divergence splits a sequence into several branches, a convergence joins them back. A single bar means OR, a double bar means AND.","definitionHtml":"<p>A divergence splits a sequence into several branches, a convergence joins them back. A single bar means OR, a double bar means AND.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"divergence and convergence","figure":{"src":"/glossary/grafcet/divergences-en.svg","alt":"Four junctions, left to right: OR divergence (one bar), OR convergence, AND divergence (double bar), AND convergence.","width":420},"related":[{"id":"or-divergence","term":"OR divergence"},{"id":"and-divergence","term":"AND divergence"},{"id":"convergence","term":"Convergence"},{"id":"branch","term":"Branch"}]},{"id":"double-coil","section":"ladder","term":"Double coil","aliases":[],"definition":"A common mistake: writing the same variable with two coils. Only the last network executed counts, which hides the first.","definitionHtml":"<p>A common mistake: writing the same variable with two coils. Only the last network executed counts, which hides the first.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"double coil","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"network","term":"Network"},{"id":"execution-order","term":"Execution order"}]},{"id":"edge","section":"general","term":"Edge","aliases":[],"definition":"The precise moment a signal changes value: rising edge (false to true) or falling edge (true to false).","definitionHtml":"<p>The precise moment a signal changes value: rising edge (false to true) or falling edge (true to false).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>An edge lasts a single cycle: it is used to react only once to a press.</p>\n","searchText":"edge","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"rising-edge","term":"Rising edge"},{"id":"falling-edge","term":"Falling edge"},{"id":"edge-contacts","term":"Edge contacts P and N"}]},{"id":"edge-contacts","section":"ladder","term":"Edge contacts P and N","aliases":["P contact","N contact","rising edge","falling edge"],"definition":"A P contact conducts for a single cycle, on the rising edge of its variable; an N contact does so on the falling edge.","definitionHtml":"<p>A P contact conducts for a single cycle, on the rising edge of its variable; an N contact does so on the falling edge.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>They are used to react only once to a press.</p>\n","searchText":"edge contacts p and n","figure":{"src":"/glossary/ladder/edge-contacts-en.svg","alt":"Two contacts: a P contact marked with the letter P and an N contact marked with the letter N.","width":360},"related":[{"id":"edge","term":"Edge"},{"id":"rising-edge","term":"Rising edge"},{"id":"falling-edge","term":"Falling edge"}]},{"id":"evolution","section":"grafcet","term":"Evolution","aliases":["crossing","crossing a transition","firing"],"definition":"Crossing a transition: when the upstream step is active and the receptivity is true, the upstream step deactivates and the downstream step activates.","definitionHtml":"<p>Crossing a transition: when the upstream step is active and the receptivity is true, the upstream step deactivates and the downstream step activates.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>The upstream step must be active AND the receptivity true: if either is missing, nothing moves.</p>\n","searchText":"evolution","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"transition","term":"Transition"},{"id":"upstream-downstream","term":"Upstream, downstream"}]},{"id":"exclusivity","section":"grafcet","term":"Exclusivity","aliases":["mutual exclusion"],"definition":"A property of the branches of an OR divergence whose receptivities cannot be true at the same time.","definitionHtml":"<p>A property of the branches of an OR divergence whose receptivities cannot be true at the same time.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>Without exclusivity, several branches can start at once: the Studomate analysis flags it.</p>\n","searchText":"exclusivity","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"or-divergence","term":"OR divergence"}]},{"id":"execution-order","section":"general","term":"Execution order","aliases":[],"definition":"The rule for reading the program: networks run from top to bottom, and GRAFCETs run before Ladder.","definitionHtml":"<p>The rule for reading the program: networks run from top to bottom, and GRAFCETs run before Ladder.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>A network placed lower already sees the result of the networks above it within the same cycle. If two networks write the same variable, the last one executed wins.</p>\n","searchText":"execution order","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"scan-cycle","term":"Scan cycle"}]},{"id":"falling-edge","section":"general","term":"Falling edge","aliases":[],"definition":"A signal going from true to false, detected during a single cycle.","definitionHtml":"<p>A signal going from true to false, detected during a single cycle.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"falling edge","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"edge","term":"Edge"},{"id":"rising-edge","term":"Rising edge"}]},{"id":"function-block","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Function block","aliases":["block"],"definition":"A Ladder rectangle that performs a ready-made function (timing, counting, calculation) from input pins on the left and output pins on the right.","definitionHtml":"<p>A Ladder rectangle that performs a ready-made function (timing, counting, calculation) from input pins on the left and output pins on the right.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"function block","figure":{"src":"/glossary/ladder-advanced/timer-block.svg","alt":"A TON block: pins IN and PT on the left, pins Q and ET on the right.","width":300},"related":[{"id":"timer","term":"Timer"},{"id":"counter","term":"Counter"},{"id":"instance","term":"Instance"}]},{"id":"hysteresis","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Hysteresis","aliases":[],"definition":"A gap between the switch-on threshold and the switch-off threshold, to prevent an output from flickering when the measurement oscillates around one value.","definitionHtml":"<p>A gap between the switch-on threshold and the switch-off threshold, to prevent an output from flickering when the measurement oscillates around one value.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"hysteresis","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"scaling","term":"Scaling"}]},{"id":"initial-step","section":"grafcet","term":"Initial step","aliases":[],"definition":"A step with a double outline, active at power-up or after a reset. A GRAFCET has at least one.","definitionHtml":"<p>A step with a double outline, active at power-up or after a reset. A GRAFCET has at least one.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"initial step","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"step","term":"Step"},{"id":"reinitialize","term":"Reset"}]},{"id":"input","section":"general","term":"Input","aliases":[],"definition":"A variable read by the program and driven by the outside world: button, switch, sensor.","definitionHtml":"<p>A variable read by the program and driven by the outside world: button, switch, sensor.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>In the program, an input is read with a contact. The program cannot write it.</p>\n","searchText":"input","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"output","term":"Output"},{"id":"push-button","term":"Push button"},{"id":"switch","term":"Switch"},{"id":"wiring","term":"Wiring: normally open (NO) and normally closed (NC)"}]},{"id":"instance","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Instance","aliases":[],"definition":"One copy of a function block, with its own state: two TON timers are two independent instances.","definitionHtml":"<p>One copy of a function block, with its own state: two TON timers are two independent instances.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"instance","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"function-block","term":"Function block"},{"id":"timer","term":"Timer"},{"id":"counter","term":"Counter"}]},{"id":"interlock","section":"ladder","term":"Interlock","aliases":["mutual interlock"],"definition":"A condition that forbids two outputs from being active at the same time, like the two directions of a motor: each can start only if the other is off.","definitionHtml":"<p>A condition that forbids two outputs from being active at the same time, like the two directions of a motor: each can start only if the other is off.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"interlock","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"self-holding","term":"Self-holding"}]},{"id":"internal-memory","section":"ladder","term":"Internal memory","aliases":["memory","memory bit"],"definition":"A variable that is neither an input nor an output: the program uses it to remember a state between two cycles.","definitionHtml":"<p>A variable that is neither an input nor an output: the program uses it to remember a state between two cycles.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"internal memory","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"variable","term":"Variable"},{"id":"set-reset","term":"S and R coils"},{"id":"retentive","term":"Retentive memory"}]},{"id":"ladder","section":"ladder","term":"Ladder","aliases":["LD","ladder diagram","relay diagram"],"definition":"A graphical PLC programming language: contacts on the left (the conditions) drive a coil on the right (the action).","definitionHtml":"<p>A graphical PLC programming language: contacts on the left (the conditions) drive a coil on the right (the action).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>It descends from the relay diagram and is written « LD » in the IEC 61131-3 standard.</p>\n","searchText":"ladder","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"network","term":"Network"},{"id":"contact","term":"Contact"},{"id":"coil","term":"Coil"}]},{"id":"limit-switch","section":"general","term":"Limit switch","aliases":["end stop"],"definition":"A sensor operated mechanically when a moving part (gate, cylinder) reaches the end of its travel.","definitionHtml":"<p>A sensor operated mechanically when a moving part (gate, cylinder) reaches the end of its travel.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"limit switch","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"input","term":"Input"}]},{"id":"main","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Main","aliases":["main program"],"definition":"The main program of a project, run on every cycle. It calls the subprograms and cannot be excluded from execution.","definitionHtml":"<p>The main program of a project, run on every cycle. It calls the subprograms and cannot be excluded from execution.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"main","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"subprogram","term":"Subprogram"}]},{"id":"mnemonic","section":"general","term":"Mnemonic","aliases":["variable name"],"definition":"The short, meaningful name of a variable (pump, stop), which programs use to refer to it. An address (%I0.1) can be added to link the variable to physical hardware.","definitionHtml":"<p>The short, meaningful name of a variable (<code>pump</code>, <code>stop</code>), which programs use to refer to it. An address (<code>%I0.1</code>) can be added to link the variable to physical hardware.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"mnemonic","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"variable","term":"Variable"}]},{"id":"network","section":"ladder","term":"Network","aliases":["rung","section"],"definition":"A block of the Ladder program, bounded by its two rails. It contains lines of contacts leading to coils. In the simplest case, a single line: contacts on the left, a coil on the right. It is read from left to right.","definitionHtml":"<p>A block of the Ladder program, bounded by its two rails. It contains lines of contacts leading to coils. In the simplest case, a single line: contacts on the left, a coil on the right. It is read from left to right.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>If the contact path of a line lets current through, the coil is activated.</p>\n","searchText":"network","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"contact","term":"Contact"},{"id":"coil","term":"Coil"},{"id":"execution-order","term":"Execution order"}]},{"id":"not","section":"general","term":"NOT","aliases":["inversion"],"definition":"An operator that inverts a condition: true becomes false, false becomes true.","definitionHtml":"<p>An operator that inverts a condition: true becomes false, false becomes true.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>In Ladder, NOT corresponds to an NC contact.</p>\n","searchText":"not","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"and","term":"AND"},{"id":"or","term":"OR"}]},{"id":"or","section":"general","term":"OR","aliases":["in parallel"],"definition":"An operator that is true as soon as one of its conditions is true.","definitionHtml":"<p>An operator that is true as soon as one of its conditions is true.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>In Ladder, OR corresponds to contacts in parallel.</p>\n","searchText":"or","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"and","term":"AND"},{"id":"not","term":"NOT"},{"id":"series-parallel","term":"Contacts in series and in parallel"}]},{"id":"or-divergence","section":"grafcet","term":"OR divergence","aliases":["sequence selection"],"definition":"A point where the sequence splits into several paths of which only one is taken, depending on which receptivity becomes true first.","definitionHtml":"<p>A point where the sequence splits into several paths of which only one is taken, depending on which receptivity becomes true first.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>The branch receptivities must be mutually exclusive.</p>\n","searchText":"or divergence","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"and-divergence","term":"AND divergence"},{"id":"exclusivity","term":"Exclusivity"},{"id":"divergences","term":"Divergence and convergence"}]},{"id":"output","section":"general","term":"Output","aliases":[],"definition":"A variable written by the program to drive a lamp, a contactor, a valve or a motor.","definitionHtml":"<p>A variable written by the program to drive a lamp, a contactor, a valve or a motor.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>In Ladder an output is driven by a coil; in GRAFCET, by an action.</p>\n","searchText":"output","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"input","term":"Input"},{"id":"contactor","term":"Contactor"}]},{"id":"overflow","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Overflow","aliases":["wrap-around"],"definition":"A result that goes out of the range of its type: an INT passing 32767 wraps around to the low bound.","definitionHtml":"<p>A result that goes out of the range of its type: an INT passing 32767 wraps around to the low bound.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"overflow","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"data-type","term":"Type"}]},{"id":"plc","section":"general","term":"PLC","aliases":["programmable logic controller","programmable controller"],"definition":"A small industrial computer that reads inputs (buttons, sensors), runs a program, then drives outputs (lamps, contactors, valves).","definitionHtml":"<p>A small industrial computer that reads inputs (buttons, sensors), runs a program, then drives outputs (lamps, contactors, valves).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>It endlessly repeats the same loop, the scan cycle. In Studomate, the program is written in GRAFCET and Ladder.</p>\n","searchText":"plc","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"scan-cycle","term":"Scan cycle"},{"id":"input","term":"Input"},{"id":"output","term":"Output"}]},{"id":"preset-value","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Preset value","aliases":["PV","preset"],"definition":"The target value of a counter (PV pin). The Q output of a CTU becomes true when the count CV reaches PV.","definitionHtml":"<p>The target value of a counter (PV pin). The Q output of a CTU becomes true when the count CV reaches PV.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"preset value","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"counter","term":"Counter"}]},{"id":"push-button","section":"general","term":"Push button","aliases":[],"definition":"A control device that changes state while pressed and returns to rest by itself when released.","definitionHtml":"<p>A control device that changes state while pressed and returns to rest by itself when released.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"push button","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"switch","term":"Switch"},{"id":"wiring","term":"Wiring: normally open (NO) and normally closed (NC)"},{"id":"input","term":"Input"}]},{"id":"rails","section":"ladder","term":"Rails","aliases":["left rail","right rail"],"definition":"The two vertical lines framing a Ladder network: the notional current flows from the left rail to the right rail.","definitionHtml":"<p>The two vertical lines framing a Ladder network: the notional current flows from the left rail to the right rail.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"rails","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"network","term":"Network"}]},{"id":"receptivity","section":"grafcet","term":"Receptivity","aliases":["transition condition"],"definition":"The crossing condition of a transition: a true-or-false expression, such as end1 or cycle_start AND NOT stop.","definitionHtml":"<p>The crossing condition of a transition: a true-or-false expression, such as <code>end1</code> or <code>cycle_start AND NOT stop</code>.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>A receptivity can contain a timer or an edge.</p>\n","searchText":"receptivity","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"transition","term":"Transition"},{"id":"evolution","term":"Evolution"}]},{"id":"reinitialize","section":"grafcet","term":"Reset","aliases":["reinitialize","GRAFCET reset"],"definition":"Put the whole GRAFCET back in its starting state: all steps inactive except the initial step, which becomes active again.","definitionHtml":"<p>Put the whole GRAFCET back in its starting state: all steps inactive except the initial step, which becomes active again.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"reset","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"initial-step","term":"Initial step"}]},{"id":"retentive","section":"ladder","term":"Retentive memory","aliases":["retentivity"],"definition":"A memory that keeps its value after a power loss or a restart, unlike an ordinary memory that restarts at 0.","definitionHtml":"<p>A memory that keeps its value after a power loss or a restart, unlike an ordinary memory that restarts at 0.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"retentive memory","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"set-reset","term":"S and R coils"},{"id":"internal-memory","term":"Internal memory"}]},{"id":"rising-edge","section":"general","term":"Rising edge","aliases":[],"definition":"A signal going from false to true, detected during a single cycle.","definitionHtml":"<p>A signal going from false to true, detected during a single cycle.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"rising edge","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"edge","term":"Edge"},{"id":"falling-edge","term":"Falling edge"}]},{"id":"set-reset","section":"ladder","term":"S and R coils","aliases":["Set","Reset","latch","set to 1","set to 0"],"definition":"An S (Set) coil sets its variable to 1 and leaves it; an R (Reset) coil sets it back to 0. Between orders, the variable keeps its value.","definitionHtml":"<p>An S (Set) coil sets its variable to 1 and leaves it; an R (Reset) coil sets it back to 0. Between orders, the variable keeps its value.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>The last network executed wins if both are active together.</p>\n","searchText":"s and r coils","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"internal-memory","term":"Internal memory"},{"id":"self-holding","term":"Self-holding"},{"id":"retentive","term":"Retentive memory"}]},{"id":"scaling","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Scaling","aliases":["raw value"],"definition":"A calculation that converts the raw value of an analog sensor into a physical quantity (temperature, level), usually through a straight line.","definitionHtml":"<p>A calculation that converts the raw value of an analog sensor into a physical quantity (temperature, level), usually through a straight line.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"scaling","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"data-type","term":"Type"}]},{"id":"scan-cycle","section":"general","term":"Scan cycle","aliases":["PLC cycle","scan"],"definition":"The loop a PLC repeats endlessly, in three phases: read the inputs, run the program, write the outputs.","definitionHtml":"<p>The loop a PLC repeats endlessly, in three phases: read the inputs, run the program, write the outputs.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>A cycle lasts a few milliseconds. While the program runs, inputs are frozen: they keep the value read at the start of the cycle.</p>\n","searchText":"scan cycle","figure":{"src":"/glossary/general/scan-cycle-en.svg","alt":"The scan cycle as three blocks linked by arrows: read inputs, run the program, write outputs, then back to the start.","width":520},"related":[{"id":"plc","term":"PLC"},{"id":"execution-order","term":"Execution order"}]},{"id":"self-holding","section":"ladder","term":"Self-holding","aliases":["latching","seal-in"],"definition":"A circuit where a contact of the coil itself is placed in parallel with the start button: the output stays on after the button is released.","definitionHtml":"<p>A circuit where a contact of the coil itself is placed in parallel with the start button: the output stays on after the button is released.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>With the stop in series after the parallel, the stop has priority.</p>\n","searchText":"self-holding","figure":{"src":"/glossary/ladder/self-holding-en.svg","alt":"A network: `start` in parallel with `pump`, then an NC contact `stop` in series, to the `pump` coil.","width":420},"related":[{"id":"priority-stop","term":"Stop priority"},{"id":"set-reset","term":"S and R coils"},{"id":"internal-memory","term":"Internal memory"}]},{"id":"step","section":"grafcet","term":"Step","aliases":[],"definition":"A numbered square representing a stable state of the system. It is active or inactive; an active step is shown with a coloured background in the editor.","definitionHtml":"<p>A numbered square representing a stable state of the system. It is active or inactive; an active step is shown with a coloured background in the editor.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>The <code>Xn</code> variable of a step is TRUE while step n is active.</p>\n","searchText":"step","figure":{"src":"/glossary/grafcet/step-en.svg","alt":"Three steps: an inactive step (number 1), an active step (number 2, green background) and an initial step (number 0, double outline).","width":380},"related":[{"id":"initial-step","term":"Initial step"},{"id":"action","term":"Action"},{"id":"transition","term":"Transition"},{"id":"step-variable","term":"Step variable (Xn)"}]},{"id":"step-variable","section":"grafcet","term":"Step variable (Xn)","aliases":["Xn","X2"],"definition":"A logic variable tied to step n: it is TRUE when the step is active (X2 = TRUE).","definitionHtml":"<p>A logic variable tied to step n: it is TRUE when the step is active (<code>X2 = TRUE</code>).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>It is used in a receptivity or in a Ladder program to know where the sequence stands.</p>\n","searchText":"step variable (xn)","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"step","term":"Step"}]},{"id":"priority-stop","section":"ladder","term":"Stop priority","aliases":["start priority"],"definition":"A self-holding circuit where the stop wins if start and stop are operated together. Priority depends on the order of the contacts.","definitionHtml":"<p>A self-holding circuit where the stop wins if start and stop are operated together. Priority depends on the order of the contacts.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"stop priority","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"self-holding","term":"Self-holding"}]},{"id":"set-action","section":"grafcet","term":"Stored action","aliases":["Set","Reset","Set action"],"definition":"An action whose variable stays true when the step deactivates, until another action sets it back to false (Reset).","definitionHtml":"<p>An action whose variable stays true when the step deactivates, until another action sets it back to false (Reset).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"stored action","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"action","term":"Action"},{"id":"set-reset","term":"S and R coils"}]},{"id":"subprogram","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Subprogram","aliases":["subprogram call"],"definition":"A program called from another one through a call block. It lets a project be split into readable, reusable parts.","definitionHtml":"<p>A program called from another one through a call block. It lets a project be split into readable, reusable parts.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"subprogram","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"main","term":"Main"},{"id":"function-block","term":"Function block"}]},{"id":"switch","section":"general","term":"Switch","aliases":["maintained switch","toggle switch"],"definition":"A control device that keeps its position after being operated: it stays on until switched back.","definitionHtml":"<p>A control device that keeps its position after being operated: it stays on until switched back.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"switch","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"push-button","term":"Push button"},{"id":"wiring","term":"Wiring: normally open (NO) and normally closed (NC)"},{"id":"input","term":"Input"}]},{"id":"system-time-bases","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"System time bases","aliases":["_SYS_TB","system clock"],"definition":"Read-only variables provided by Studomate (prefix _SYS_) that alternate between true and false at a fixed rate, from 200 ms to 2 s, for example to blink a lamp.","definitionHtml":"<p>Read-only variables provided by Studomate (prefix <code>_SYS_</code>) that alternate between true and false at a fixed rate, from 200 ms to 2 s, for example to blink a lamp.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"system time bases","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"timer","term":"Timer"}]},{"id":"timer","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Timer","aliases":["timer block"],"definition":"A block that measures a duration. It receives an input IN and a duration PT (the preset time), and its output Q responds according to the type: TON, TOF or TP.","definitionHtml":"<p>A block that measures a duration. It receives an input IN and a duration PT (the preset time), and its output Q responds according to the type: TON, TOF or TP.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"timer","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"ton","term":"TON"},{"id":"tof","term":"TOF"},{"id":"tp","term":"TP"},{"id":"system-time-bases","term":"System time bases"}]},{"id":"chronogram","section":"general","term":"Timing diagram","aliases":["chronogram"],"definition":"A chart showing how several signals change over time, stacked on the same time axis.","definitionHtml":"<p>A chart showing how several signals change over time, stacked on the same time axis.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"timing diagram","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"scan-cycle","term":"Scan cycle"}]},{"id":"tof","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"TOF","aliases":["off-delay timer"],"definition":"Off-delay timer: Q becomes true as soon as IN is true and stays true for the duration PT after IN has fallen.","definitionHtml":"<p>Off-delay timer: Q becomes true as soon as IN is true and stays true for the duration PT after IN has fallen.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"tof","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"timer","term":"Timer"},{"id":"ton","term":"TON"},{"id":"tp","term":"TP"}]},{"id":"toggle","section":"ladder","term":"Toggle circuit","aliases":["latching relay","flip-flop"],"definition":"A circuit where each press of a button inverts the state of an output: one press turns it on, the next turns it off.","definitionHtml":"<p>A circuit where each press of a button inverts the state of an output: one press turns it on, the next turns it off.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"toggle circuit","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"edge-contacts","term":"Edge contacts P and N"},{"id":"set-reset","term":"S and R coils"}]},{"id":"ton","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"TON","aliases":["on-delay timer"],"definition":"On-delay timer: output Q becomes true when IN has stayed true for the whole duration PT, and falls as soon as IN falls.","definitionHtml":"<p>On-delay timer: output Q becomes true when IN has stayed true for the whole duration PT, and falls as soon as IN falls.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"ton","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"timer","term":"Timer"},{"id":"tof","term":"TOF"},{"id":"tp","term":"TP"}]},{"id":"tp","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"TP","aliases":["pulse timer"],"definition":"Pulse timer: a rising edge on IN triggers an output Q that is true for exactly the duration PT, whatever IN does afterwards.","definitionHtml":"<p>Pulse timer: a rising edge on IN triggers an output Q that is true for exactly the duration PT, whatever IN does afterwards.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"tp","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"timer","term":"Timer"},{"id":"ton","term":"TON"},{"id":"tof","term":"TOF"}]},{"id":"transition","section":"grafcet","term":"Transition","aliases":[],"definition":"A small horizontal bar linking two steps and carrying a receptivity: the condition to meet to go from one to the other.","definitionHtml":"<p>A small horizontal bar linking two steps and carrying a receptivity: the condition to meet to go from one to the other.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"transition","figure":{"src":"/glossary/grafcet/transition-en.svg","alt":"Two steps linked by a transition, with the receptivity `end1` to the right of the bar.","width":300},"related":[{"id":"receptivity","term":"Receptivity"},{"id":"evolution","term":"Evolution"},{"id":"step","term":"Step"}]},{"id":"truth-table","section":"general","term":"Truth table","aliases":[],"definition":"A table giving the value of a logic expression for every combination of its variables (0 = false, 1 = true).","definitionHtml":"<p>A table giving the value of a logic expression for every combination of its variables (0 = false, 1 = true).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"truth table","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"and","term":"AND"},{"id":"or","term":"OR"},{"id":"not","term":"NOT"}]},{"id":"data-type","section":"ladder-advanced","term":"Type","aliases":["BOOL","INT","DINT","REAL","variable type"],"definition":"The nature of a variable's value: BOOL (true or false), INT and DINT (16-bit and 32-bit integers), REAL (floating-point number).","definitionHtml":"<p>The nature of a variable&#39;s value: BOOL (true or false), INT and DINT (16-bit and 32-bit integers), REAL (floating-point number).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>Each type has its own range of values and calculation rules.</p>\n","searchText":"type","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"conversion","term":"Conversion"},{"id":"overflow","term":"Overflow"}]},{"id":"upstream-downstream","section":"grafcet","term":"Upstream, downstream","aliases":[],"definition":"Before and after, in the reading direction of the GRAFCET (top to bottom). The upstream step precedes a transition, the downstream step follows it.","definitionHtml":"<p>Before and after, in the reading direction of the GRAFCET (top to bottom). The upstream step precedes a transition, the downstream step follows it.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"","searchText":"upstream, downstream","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"evolution","term":"Evolution"}]},{"id":"variable","section":"general","term":"Variable","aliases":[],"definition":"A named piece of data handled by the program: an input, an output or an internal memory. A logic variable is TRUE or FALSE (1 or 0).","definitionHtml":"<p>A named piece of data handled by the program: an input, an output or an internal memory. A logic variable is TRUE or FALSE (1 or 0).</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>Studomate declares variables in the variables table, shared between GRAFCET, Ladder and HMI.</p>\n","searchText":"variable","figure":"$undefined","related":[{"id":"mnemonic","term":"Mnemonic"},{"id":"input","term":"Input"},{"id":"output","term":"Output"}]},{"id":"wiring","section":"general","term":"Wiring: normally open (NO) and normally closed (NC)","aliases":["NO","NC","normally open","normally closed"],"definition":"The way a button or sensor is connected. Wired normally open (NO), it is 0 at rest and 1 when operated; wired normally closed (NC), it is 1 at rest and 0 when operated.","definitionHtml":"<p>The way a button or sensor is connected. Wired normally open (NO), it is 0 at rest and 1 when operated; wired normally closed (NC), it is 1 at rest and 0 when operated.</p>\n","detailsHtml":"<p>The physical wiring and the contact chosen in the program are two different things.</p>\n","searchText":"wiring: normally open (no) and normally closed (nc)","figure":{"src":"/glossary/general/wiring-no-nc-en.svg","alt":"Two buttons: the normally open one (NO) is 0 at rest and 1 when pressed, the normally closed one (NC) is 1 at rest and 0 when pressed.","width":460},"related":[{"id":"contact","term":"Contact"},{"id":"input","term":"Input"},{"id":"push-button","term":"Push button"}]}],"labels":{"searchLabel":"Search for a term","searchPlaceholder":"Step, contact, TON, edge...","filterLabel":"Filter by notation","filterAll":"All","noResults":"No term matches your search.","aliasesLabel":"Also called","relatedLabel":"See also","resultsOne":"1 term","resultsOther":"{count} terms"}}]
